k__\" and printed, the session going on, but SystemExit,"] [390 1 "// whose status ends the run (exit true), as pymain_err_print."] [395 2 "// site, which CPython imports at start (pyi does not): imported here, before the REPL, so that its main sets the hook"] [396 2 "// (enablerlcompleter, but under -I)"] [420 1 "// runStartup is pymain_run_startup (Modules/main.c; queue 293), before the REPL on stdin when there is no code to run:"] [421 1 "// the file PYTHONSTARTUP names (not under -E or -I) run in __main__'s namespace g as _PyRun_SimpleFileObject runs it,"] [422 1 "// its __file__ set for the run, an error printed (sys.excepthook) and the session going on; SystemExit ends the run"] [423 1 "// with its status (exit true), as PyErr_Print's handle_system_exit; a file that does not open: \"Could not open"] [424 1 "// PYTHONSTARTUP\" and its OSError printed."] [467 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [468 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [471 1 "// mModeFile and stdinModeFile are the files bin/pyi python writes for -m and for a program read from stdin (queue 250)."] [477 1 "// startSafePath is -P (safe_path) as bin/pyi python's command line gave it (PYI_SAFE_PATH: 1 under -P or -I, 0"] [478 1 "// without, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is); -1 when not run by bin/pyi python (bin/pyi"] [479 1 "// run's programs and the check's driver, whose sys.flags.safe_path is the reference driver's -P)."] [500 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [501 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [506 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [507 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [508 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when t